fixture up_strike_never_cancels_itself
doc (movement review 4, M6) BUILD.md s6 Taper, Up: "Cancel into: Dash from f 4, air attack any frame": into another air strike (a side or down-strike), never into itself. An up press every 3 frames in the air used to restart the up-strike each time, a fresh active box every third frame (7 up-strikes in 21 frames, where one is 16); now the strike runs its frames and the last buffered press starts the next one.
room test/flat
spawn 400 200
frames 24
input
  0 U !attack
  1..2 U
  3 U !attack
  4..5 U
  6 U !attack
  7..8 U
  9 U !attack
  10..11 U
  12 U !attack
  13..14 U
  15 U !attack
  16..17 U
  18 U !attack
  19..23 U
end
expect
  # One up-strike runs its 16 frames: the up presses during it are not a new up-strike. The last
  # one, still in the buffer when it ends, starts the next.
  at 0 action=up action_frame=1 event.attack=1
  never 1..15 event.attack=1
  at 16 action=up action_frame=1 event.attack=1
  during 2..6 strike=1
  never 7..17 strike=1
end
